{
  "slug": "specclaw",
  "name": "Specclaw",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Spec-driven development framework for Claude Code. Manages the propose → plan → build → verify → pr lifecycle with structured proposals, specs, designs, task lists, and GitHub/Azure DevOps/Jira integrations.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **19 skills** and **2 agents**.\n\n- **Skills** (19): `archive` (Move a completed change to .specclaw/changes/archive/ with a date prefix), `auth-azdo` (Interactive setup for Azure DevOps authentication), `auth-jira` (Interactive setup for Jira authentication), `author-spec` (Interactively co-author spec.md for an approved proposal via the spec-author subagent), `auto` (Run the propose → plan → build → verify lifecycle autonomously across the queue of active changes), `azdo-issue` (Create or update an Azure Boards Work Item that mirrors this proposal), `build` (Implement planned tasks by executing them wave-by-wave, committing each, and logging errors and learnings), `context` (Manage the project's living context document (.specclaw/context.md)), and 11 more\n- **Agents** (2): `code-reviewer` (Reviews changed files for a specclaw change across 10 quality dimensions (correctness, security, YAGNI/simplicity, one-liner opportunities, naming, complexity,…), `spec-author` (Interactively co-authors a high-quality spec.md for a specclaw change)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install specclaw@claude-community` from `chan4lk/specclaw` (`plugins/specclaw`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 19,
    "agent": 2
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
